    {
      "question": "e-5557",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "9c6ef28e5edaafddb8a7afef778ce000b35009d9e1ed902f926d77e53dece73f",
      "new_sha256": "5a4eec0898a48b66508b4305790b3bf509704059c8b698df07b2e18b61f964ea",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5557",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Since $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v},$ we also have that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $4\\mathbf{v}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+4v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+\u20164v{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016u+4v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+(4\u2016v\u2016)^{2} \\\\ \u2016u+4v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+16\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+16(6)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+576 \\\\ \u2016u{\u2016}^{2} & =625-576 \\\\ \u2016u{\u2016}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=\\Vert\\mathbf{u}\\Vert^2=49.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5557.json",
          "file_sha256": "e28fb05018f3a3fabd681b35e62b244f9f05c85e73d4defb1a40fb653cb50912"
        }
      ],
