      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5559",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Let the vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}|^2+5\\Vert\\mathbf{v}+\\mathbf{w}\\Vert^2=29$ and $\\| \\mathbf{u} \\|  = \\| \\mathbf{w} \\| = 2$, then what is the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert?$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5559.json",
          "file_sha256": "62f3e1d27ad9ff46f5a1555ccf4a0a78819d10eac567ae52c2fe65417d47a5e4"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1466,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1467
    },
    {
      "question": "e-5559",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "ffb67152a037cb4bfc8002189921ab83697584d932c946a090e7b0be36ccc514",
      "new_sha256": "73fb9eb9cef15209fa0bc762ccd9224b5d03f46acb2422023b291824cca084bc",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5559",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}\\cdot \u2016v\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & =4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{w}$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} & =4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5(\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016w{\u2016}^{2}) \\\\  & \\le 4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5(\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & \\le 9\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+20 \\\\ 9 & \\le 9\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ 1 & \\le \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert^2$ implies that $1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$. Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$ is $1.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/example-5559.json",
          "file_sha256": "62f3e1d27ad9ff46f5a1555ccf4a0a78819d10eac567ae52c2fe65417d47a5e4"
        }
      ],
